Introduction to JavaScript:
4.Have you heard of JavaScript? If yes, what is JavaScript, and why is it crucial for building interactive websites?
Section 4: Introduction to React and Node.js

Yes, javaScript is a programming language primarily used to make web pages interactive and dynamic. It allows developers to respond to user actions, manipulate HTML content, validate forms, communicate with servers, and update page content without reloading the entire page.
For example, if I create a button using HTML and style it with CSS, JavaScript enables me to define what happens when the user clicks that button. It can trigger an action, display a message, fetch data, or modify the content of the page dynamically.


